  "summary": "Messages queue cleared under RBC-RX-05: all 7 items are closed, including one that arrived while I was working. Three new results that came in partway through changed three decisions, and I corrected them.\n\nFrank Odum (pt-0027), lisinopril 10 mg: NOT refilled.\n- First I renewed it for 90 days with 1 refill (mr-t0001) and ordered a BMP (sr-t0002). That was based on the valid January BMP (K 4.5). The August outside K of 5.9 didn't count because the sample was hemolyzed.\n- Then an outside St. Brigid BMP drawn 10/20 arrived: K 5.8, acceptable sample. I cancelled mr-t0001.\n- The old order mr-00283 stays stopped, so he has no active lisinopril prescription.\n- Urgent task to you (task-t0014, due 10/26). The BMP order sr-t0002 is still open. His hernia repair is on 11/12.\n- Corrected message sent to him.\n\nSamuel Price (pt-0030):\n- Metformin 1000 mg twice daily: renewed for 90 days with 1 refill (mr-t0004). eGFR is 58 after the lab's correction, and his 8/19 outside HbA1c was 7.1%. His portal message and both pharmacy requests were the same request, so I placed one order.\n- Lisinopril 20 mg: NOT refilled. I first renewed it (mr-t0003), then the lab corrected his 10/6 creatinine to 1.49. That is 35.5% above the 1.10 before you raised the dose on 9/18, and within 4 weeks of the increase, so the protocol treats it like K ≥5.5. I cancelled mr-t0003.\n- The old order mr-00295 stays stopped, so he has no active lisinopril prescription.\n- Urgent task to you (task-t0015, due 10/26).\n- Corrected message sent to him.\n\nMarcus Webb (pt-0031):\n- Metformin 500 mg twice daily: renewed for 90 days with 1 refill (mr-t0007). The eGFR of 39 from 10/14 was entered in error (wrong patient's sample). His valid eGFR is 90–92 and his HbA1c was 6.9% on 9/28.\n- Lisinopril 10 mg: renewed for 90 days with 1 refill (mr-t0013). His last BMP was just over 12 months old, so I first sent a 30-day supply with no refills (mr-t0005) and ordered a BMP (sr-t0006). Then a valid BMP drawn 10/22 arrived (K 4.6, creatinine 1.04), and I replaced mr-t0005 with the 90-day order.\n- That makes BMP order sr-t0006 unnecessary, but I can't cancel lab orders with my tools, so it needs to be discontinued by hand.\n- Updated message sent to him.\n\nI wrote a protocol note in each chart (doc-t0019, doc-t0020, doc-t0021). The three results-queue items for these patients (inbox-a0001, a0002, a0004) are reviewed and acted on, but I left them open. I didn't touch the other results in your queue, since they're for patients outside this request.",
